{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"paralysed-eminent-capybara","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Class\n\n**217 backslashed-path occurrences** in job `100874330553`. The clearest specimen:\n\n```\nassert 'src/rebar/live.py:1' in 'criteria vocabulary check failed:\\nsrc\\rebar\\live.py:1: deprecated vocabula…'\n```\n\nThis is NOT merely a test-assertion problem. rebar emits repo-relative paths into **user- and\nmachine-facing artifacts** — criteria-vocabulary diagnostics, review findings, file-impact entries,\ncommit-trailer scans — and those paths are consumed as strings and compared against forward-slash\nforms. On Windows they render with `\\`, so the artifact itself differs by platform.\n\n## What the fix must decide\n\nRepo-relative paths in rebar's **output** should be normalised to forward slashes at the rendering\nboundary — the same convention git itself uses — rather than each assertion being taught to accept\nboth. Fixing this in the assertions would leave the real artifact platform-dependent, which is the\ndefect. Locate the rendering boundaries (the diagnostic formatters, the file-impact writer, the\nreview-finding serialiser) and normalise there.\n\nNote this class was **not** in the bug's original class list; it was found by re-reading the log for\nthis decomposition. It is the largest non-`lock.py` class by raw occurrence count.\n\n## Blocked by S1\n\n## Proving command\n\n```\nuv run --no-sync pytest tests/unit/test_cli_body_guard.py tests/unit/test_code_review_artifact.py \\\n  tests/unit/test_pai_output.py -p no:cacheprovider -q\n```\non `windows-latest`, plus a cross-platform artifact-equality proof: a test that renders a\nrepo-relative path and asserts the rendered form contains `/` and no `\\`, so it fails on Windows if\nthe normalisation is removed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Repo-relative paths in rebar's rendered output use `/` on every platform.\n2. The normalisation is enforced by a test that would fail on Windows if reverted, not only by the\n   incidental passing of consumers.\n","id":"96dd-789f-a25a-41ff","parent_id":"55da-cee1-e556-4735","priority":2,"tags":["windows","portability","paths"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S4: backslash path separators leak into rendered output and assertions — 217 occurrences in the Windows sweep log"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571355673663944,"uuid":"6b245023-f720-4a26-90e2-5ef0314faff3"}